## 5.4 Soft Constraints

Minimize:

- Total travel time.
- SLA violations.
- Workload imbalance.
- Overtime.
- Customer preference violations.
- Unnecessary schedule changes.

Soft preferences must never override hard constraints.

## 5.5 Optimization Objective

Implement:

Total Cost =

(w1 × Total Travel Time)

+ (w2 × SLA Penalty)

+ (w3 × Workload Imbalance)

+ (w4 × Overtime Penalty)

+ (w5 × Customer Preference Penalty)

+ (w6 × Schedule Change Penalty)

Allow configuration of optimization weights.

Set a configurable optimization time limit.

Return the best feasible solution found within the limit.

If optimization fails, preserve the previous valid schedule.

