# 4. PROJECT-WIDE BUSINESS RULES

These rules apply to every phase:

1. Only approved technicians can receive assignments.
2. Mandatory skills and certifications must always match.
3. Customer-requested priority is not automatically verified priority.
4. Customer preferences should be honoured when feasible.
5. Round Robin must not override mandatory constraints.
6. Dijkstra calculates paths on the supplied road network, not the entire schedule.
7. OR-Tools must respect hard constraints.
8. Completed assignments must never be reassigned.
9. Ongoing work must be protected during recovery.
10. All schedule modifications must be validated before saving.
11. Failed optimization must not destroy the previous valid schedule.
12. Customers must only access their own records.
13. Technicians must only access permitted assignments and information.
14. Only authorized administrators can perform administrative actions.
15. Every important scheduling decision must be recorded and explainable.

